{
 "about": "One rule for every setting that writes to and reads from the buds. Events: tap{key,writes[[id,value]],confirm,restarts}, ack{seq,status}, report{values,seq,push} (seq set = a reply to OUR read; push true = an event the buds sent on their own; neither = any other read reply, which only updates values), tick, disconnect, reconnect. Output tokens, in order: busy:<key>:on|off, send:<id>:<value>:s<seq>, read:s<seq>, changed:<id>:<value>, toast:<key>:refused_missing|refused_now|not_changed|no_answer. The engine numbers every send and every read from s1 within a scenario. confirm: read (our read reply decides), push (the first real push for the key decides; a read reply never does; a push of the wanted value before the ack confirms at the ack), ack (the ack decides). Timeouts: 3000 ms per wait step (ack, then reply or push); 15000 ms after the last ack of a write with restarts. One operation at a time; the others wait in a queue. docs/FEATURE-SYNC.md has the rules.",
 "scenarios": [
  {
   "name": "read-confirmed: the value moves once, at our own read reply",
   "init": {
    "24": 0
   },
   "events": [
    {
     "ev": "tap",
     "key": 24,
     "writes": [
      [
       24,
       1
      ]
     ],
     "confirm": "read",
     "restarts": false,
     "now": 0,
     "expect": [
      "busy:24:on",
      "send:24:1:s1"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ev": "ack",
     "seq": 1,
     "status": 0,
     "now": 50,
     "expect": [
      "read:s2"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ev": "report",
     "values": {
      "24": 1
     },
     "seq": 2,
     "now": 120,
     "expect": [
      "changed:24:1",
      "busy:24:off"
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
